================================================================================
Headline takeaways
================================================================================
1. Forward law equivalence holds on a NONLINEAR model regardless of ESS
   level. flat-twist SV has every window dipping below 0.5N (some windows
   ESS/N < 0.04) and still max|par-seq| ~ 1e-6.

2. DEER iters per window stays CONSTANT at 2 across T=128..32768, across
   LGSSM and SV, across good and bad twists. The windowing reduced the
   genealogy-coupling problem to T/K events that DEER doesn't see.

3. Speedup plateaus ~2.7x on LGSSM scaling and ~2.5x on SV. The plateau is
   the serial scan-over-windows; bumping K is the next sweep.

4. log Z agreement is exact to ~6 significant digits (e.g. SV: seq=par
   to the printed 4 decimals).  ESS estimates agree exactly between
   seq and par.
